#
# Fetched, not committed (demos/camera_classify/fetch-model.sh)
#
# ~14 MB of binary model weights don't belong in git; fetch-model.sh
# downloads them on demand and pins them by sha256 in models.sha256.
demos/camera_classify/mobilenetv2-12.onnx
demos/camera_classify/synset.txt
# Exception: sci_gateway/c/swig/include/opencv2/core/cvstd_wrapper.hpp is a
# generated artifact -- regen.sh rewrites it from the installed OpenCV headers
# on every run and never reads the tracked copy -- but it is tracked anyway as
# a drift tripwire / audit record: `git diff` after running regen.sh shows
# whether the upstream SFINAE declaration it patches around has moved or
# changed, which would otherwise happen silently inside the ignored
# directory. Git won't apply file-level negations inside a directory an
# earlier pattern already excludes, so every path segment down to the file
# needs its own negation.
!sci_gateway/c/swig/include/
!sci_gateway/c/swig/include/opencv2/
!sci_gateway/c/swig/include/opencv2/core/
!sci_gateway/c/swig/include/opencv2/core/cvstd_wrapper.hpp
